00:49:40.910 --> 00:49:43.030
The safety of Babylon 5 is more important

00:49:43.030 --> 00:49:45.810
than any one member of her crew, am I clear?

00:50:30.830 --> 00:50:32.080
Del Varner.

00:50:32.080 --> 00:50:33.080
It's me, Eric.

00:50:33.080 --> 00:50:44.270
Remember?

00:50:44.270 --> 00:50:48.550
...present with the rest of the party when the ambassador arrived, and you can confirm

00:50:48.550 --> 00:50:51.190
that Commander Sinclair was not present, correct?

00:50:51.190 --> 00:50:53.330
Um, that is correct.

00:50:53.330 --> 00:50:55.500
He was delayed in the transport tube.

00:50:55.500 --> 00:51:00.000
But according to your own chief of security, the tube records do not reflect this.

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:11.530
is that? I don't know. Doctor, if I may, we have heard that there was a witness. Is this true? Yes

00:51:11.530 --> 00:51:21.190
and no. The information is second-hand and may or may not be admissible. The witness thinks it

00:51:21.190 --> 00:51:26.970
may have been the commander, but... Why are you withholding the name of the witness, Dr. Kyle?

00:51:26.970 --> 00:51:29.960
The witness requested anonymity.

00:51:30.960 --> 00:51:35.840
For the time being, if they should go to trial, that would, of course, change.

00:51:35.940 --> 00:51:40.970
I see. Given that the information about the location of the poison proved accurate,

00:51:41.210 --> 00:51:44.190
it seems strange that you would question the rest of the story.

00:51:45.370 --> 00:51:48.260
Ambassador Malari, do you have any questions?

00:51:50.900 --> 00:51:54.110
No, not at this time, thank you.

00:51:55.730 --> 00:52:00.000
One last thing, Doctor. You said you were finally able to analyze

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:15.870
the poison. What kind was it? Florezine. Pretty rare. Only comes from one system, the Damocles

00:52:15.870 --> 00:52:22.850
Sector. Were you aware that the Commander's woman recently returned from a trading expedition

00:52:22.850 --> 00:52:30.000
to the Damocles Sector? Just a minute. Commander. And that her ship, the Ulysses, docked at

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:44.550
attempted assassination. Damn it! Leave Carolyn out of this. No further questions. Okay, you're saying

00:52:44.550 --> 00:52:49.590
you don't believe what Lita Alexander saw in the ambassador's mind. Based on what? I don't trust

00:52:49.590 --> 00:52:56.030
telepaths. Never have, never will. Who knows what she really saw? And I've seen her a lot with Del

00:52:56.030 --> 00:52:59.570
Varner, the one who kept Londo from attending the reception. So?

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:03.270
check with our central it turns out Varner's got a criminal record going back

00:53:03.270 --> 00:53:06.910
five years he's been indicted three times in the last year for tech running

00:53:06.910 --> 00:53:20.850
take a look all these indictments are from the earth alliance court smuggling

00:53:20.850 --> 00:53:26.340
forbidden technology from the Vega system same again from the Proxima system

00:53:26.340 --> 00:53:30.000
exactly now the minute he sets foot on Babylon 5 he's an earth jerk

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:34.840
and subject to arrest why would he take that kind of risk there would have to be

00:53:34.840 --> 00:53:39.740
something major at stake and something else Varner promised to back Londo's

00:53:39.740 --> 00:53:43.400
bets at the casino then backed out but Varner does a lot of business with the

00:53:43.400 --> 00:53:48.140
Centauri Republic why risk alienating his clientele by burning Londo for that

00:53:48.140 --> 00:53:53.200
matter why promise to back Londo at all tech runners aren't noted for generosity

00:53:53.200 --> 00:53:57.720
no and apparently Varner's been heavily in debt he couldn't have paid Londo's

00:53:57.720 --> 00:53:58.900
debts if he wanted to

00:54:00.250 --> 00:54:05.100
just doesn't add up hmm I don't know how he fits in yet but I'll bet you a hundred

00:54:05.100 --> 00:54:10.030
credits he's involved then I think it's about time you had a little talk with

00:54:10.030 --> 00:54:26.900
mr. Varner ambassador molari I would like to discuss your vote with you the

00:54:26.900 --> 00:54:30.000
Babylon 5 Advisory Council is hereby

00:54:30.000 --> 00:54:32.430
I reconvened.

00:54:32.430 --> 00:54:36.620
Recorders are activated.

00:54:36.620 --> 00:54:41.270
Ambassador Jakar, you wish to make a motion?

00:54:41.270 --> 00:54:46.810
Commander Sinclair is a respected member of the Earth Alliance and of this council.

00:54:46.810 --> 00:54:50.790
The idea that he may have had something to do with the attempted murder of Ambassador

00:54:50.790 --> 00:54:54.550
Kosh is repellent to everyone here.

00:54:54.550 --> 00:55:00.000
Granted, there is a long history of animosity between some of our member races.

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:02.820
that Commander Sinclair personally took part

00:55:02.820 --> 00:55:04.620
in the recent Earth-Mimbori War.

00:55:04.960 --> 00:55:05.260
Grant!

00:55:05.360 --> 00:55:05.880
Ambassador.

00:55:06.620 --> 00:55:07.510
Yes, of course.

00:55:08.530 --> 00:55:11.760
I believe that it is inappropriate for this council

00:55:11.760 --> 00:55:13.780
to act as judge and jury in this matter.

00:55:14.430 --> 00:55:15.580
We are not a court,

00:55:15.660 --> 00:55:17.760
and we do not have all the facts before us.

00:55:18.680 --> 00:55:20.360
May I humbly suggest

00:55:20.360 --> 00:55:23.370
that we decline jurisdiction in this matter.

00:55:24.070 --> 00:55:27.510
This is more properly a matter for a true court of law.

00:55:28.040 --> 00:55:30.000
A court of law such as that on the Vorlox

00:55:30.060 --> 00:55:36.740
After all, the crime committed was against their ambassador.

00:55:36.740 --> 00:55:42.740
I therefore move that Commander Sinclair be remanded for transport to the Vorlon homeworld,

00:55:42.740 --> 00:55:47.620
along with whatever witnesses and evidence has been accumulated, there to stand trial

00:55:47.620 --> 00:55:50.570
on the charge of attempted murder.

00:55:50.570 --> 00:55:51.480
Ambassador!

00:55:51.480 --> 00:55:56.000
Unless it is in the interest of the Earth Alliance to try and cover up the facts.

00:55:56.000 --> 00:56:00.000
If that is the case, then Babylon 5 is a fraud!

00:56:00.120 --> 00:56:05.690
stands before this council it must be voted upon as the duly appointed representative of

00:56:05.690 --> 00:56:12.820
the non-regime i vote yes what do the rest of you have to say the earth alliance votes no

00:56:12.820 --> 00:56:28.900
ambassador delen minbari federation abstains ambassador the centauri republic

00:56:30.960 --> 00:56:32.020
Votes yes.

00:56:34.880 --> 00:56:37.970
Deadlock, Ambassador.

00:56:37.970 --> 00:56:41.640
To in favor, to opposed, or abstaining.

00:56:41.640 --> 00:56:44.530
But there is a fifth vote heard from.

00:56:44.530 --> 00:56:49.750
Two hours ago I communicated my intentions to the leaders of the Vorlon Empire.

00:56:49.750 --> 00:56:54.130
They reached a decision on the matter and asked me to cast their vote on their behalf.

00:56:54.130 --> 00:56:55.570
Votes yes.

00:56:55.570 --> 00:56:59.350
To convey Commander Sinclair to their world for trial.

00:57:00.350 --> 00:57:08.310
makes the vote three to two the motion is passed deportation is to take place within 12 hours

00:57:08.310 --> 00:57:21.600
honor this is security chief michael garibaldi i'd like to talk to you

00:57:40.810 --> 00:57:42.480
Come on in. Check around.

00:57:43.170 --> 00:57:44.380
Take the bed.

00:57:44.580 --> 00:57:45.080
Got it.

00:58:06.110 --> 00:58:06.670
Over here.

00:58:08.170 --> 00:58:10.000
DNA patent checks out, Jeff.

00:58:10.210 --> 00:58:11.420
It's Delvano, all right.

00:58:12.090 --> 00:58:13.310
Any idea when it happened?

00:58:14.020 --> 00:58:16.310
I'll have an exact time of death for you in about an hour.

00:58:17.210 --> 00:58:18.760
Someone's trying to cover their tracks.

00:58:18.900 --> 00:58:19.820
Dead-end the investigation.

00:58:21.410 --> 00:58:22.490
Barna was the key to the whole thing.

00:58:22.760 --> 00:58:24.030
What about his personal effects?

00:58:24.550 --> 00:58:26.390
I've got my people going over the place now.

00:58:27.600 --> 00:58:28.680
I'm not holding out any hope, though.

00:58:30.860 --> 00:58:32.400
- What about Ambassador Kosh?

00:58:32.400 --> 00:58:35.430
- Once I knew which poison we were dealing with,

00:58:35.430 --> 00:58:37.220
I checked around.

00:58:37.220 --> 00:58:39.900
And there is a cardiac agent to the poison.

00:58:39.900 --> 00:58:40.900
- We have some?

00:58:40.900 --> 00:58:43.460
- No, but we got something close.

00:58:43.460 --> 00:58:45.780
I'm in the process of altering the molecular structure

00:58:45.780 --> 00:58:48.040
of the compound so that it'll serve the same function.

00:58:48.040 --> 00:58:49.500
- How long?

00:58:49.500 --> 00:58:54.110
- Six, maybe seven hours.

00:58:54.110 --> 00:58:57.700
- I thought you said Kosh only had another 10 hours left.

00:58:57.700 --> 00:58:58.260
- I did.

00:59:00.060 --> 00:59:01.220
Don't make any mistakes, Ben.

00:59:05.280 --> 00:59:10.020
Dammit, maybe they were right.

00:59:10.930 --> 00:59:12.890
Maybe you got the wrong man for this job after all.

00:59:13.730 --> 00:59:15.710
With Varna gone, I don't even know where to start.

00:59:17.860 --> 00:59:19.380
Maybe you ought to turn us over to somebody else.

00:59:19.560 --> 00:59:20.920
You're talking to the wrong person.

00:59:21.060 --> 00:59:23.820
I'm scheduled to be shipped off to the Vorlon homeworld, remember?

00:59:24.770 --> 00:59:27.510
Michael, I picked you because you're right for the job.

00:59:28.120 --> 00:59:28.820
You're not politic.

00:59:30.000 --> 00:59:36.810
not subtle and sometimes you're a pain in the ass and i wouldn't have it any other way do what you

00:59:36.810 --> 00:59:54.040
have to just nail whoever's responsible come ambassador i you are upset of course i'm upset

00:59:54.040 --> 01:00:00.000
damn it dylan how can you do this to him i have done nothing right you didn't lift

01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:05.000
a finger to stop jeff from being sent to the vorlan homeworld for trial my god you didn't even vote in

01:00:05.000 --> 01:00:11.190
his favor at the council meeting you abstained i did not have all the facts i still lack some of

01:00:11.190 --> 01:00:17.820
the what you lack is a conscience i thought jeff was your friend after all he's done here for you

01:00:17.820 --> 01:00:29.220
for the station the one time he needed you you just walked away i'm sorry

01:00:30.480 --> 01:00:31.700
I can do nothing else.

01:00:32.600 --> 01:00:33.980
I have my orders.

01:00:34.970 --> 01:00:36.650
On the matter of Commander Sinclair,

01:00:37.710 --> 01:00:39.790
I'm here strictly to observe.

01:00:41.060 --> 01:00:41.940
Observe what?

01:00:50.510 --> 01:00:59.410
It's me.

01:01:04.960 --> 01:01:17.450
no oxygen mask gill implants painful to use but but efficient precisely there's been a complication

01:01:19.780 --> 01:01:26.570
lieutenant commander what is it we've lost contact with the maintenance box we sent to

01:01:26.570 --> 01:01:30.000
check on a drop of oxygen pressure in blue five level b pause

01:01:30.060 --> 01:01:31.010
- I know.

01:01:31.010 --> 01:01:32.610
- All right, get a repair crew out there,

01:01:32.610 --> 01:01:53.040
find out what's going on.

01:01:53.040 --> 01:01:57.110
- I must have got a ball day.

01:01:57.110 --> 01:01:58.360
I don't know what to say.

01:02:00.480 --> 01:02:04.650
you know I have the greatest respect for your commander Sinclair you sure have a funny way

01:02:04.650 --> 01:02:13.590
of showing it ambassador yes the vote I can see why you'd be upset by that but I didn't

01:02:13.590 --> 01:02:20.110
know you see Jakar came to me to discuss my vote huh you just went along with somebody

01:02:20.110 --> 01:02:23.470
who'd love to put you and every other Centauri on a spit and roast the whole bunch of you

01:02:23.470 --> 01:02:30.000
I had no choice back home our position status all that we

01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:38.450
have is based on family history jakar offered me an exchange my cooperation in return for evidence

01:02:38.450 --> 01:02:46.480
showing that during our rule of the non-home world certain atrocities were committed by my

01:02:46.480 --> 01:02:55.190
grandpa you know about this of course i know but what's done is done why bring it up now

01:02:55.190 --> 01:02:59.570
the point is no one else back home knows

01:03:01.820 --> 01:03:08.090
And if it were to get out, I couldn't let that happen.

01:03:11.860 --> 01:03:14.260
For what it's worth, Mr. Garibaldi, I'm sorry.

01:03:16.300 --> 01:03:18.760
I didn't think my cooperation would do him any good.

01:03:19.930 --> 01:03:23.430
Two votes for shipping Sinclair off, two against, a deadlock.

01:03:23.640 --> 01:03:26.920
I had no idea he contacted the Vorlon homeworld.

01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:33.300
If you had known, would you have done anything different?

01:03:33.300 --> 01:03:41.410
No. No, I'm afraid not.

01:03:41.410 --> 01:03:45.520
Commander Sinclair is a good man. I would hate to lose him.

01:03:45.520 --> 01:03:59.700
This is my weakness, my failure, and I'm sorry, truly sorry.

01:04:07.770 --> 01:04:11.990
Lando, thanks.

01:04:47.050 --> 01:04:48.330
Maybe I'd better come back later.

01:04:48.330 --> 01:05:00.000
No, give me a ship, turn me loose with nobody at risk but myself.

01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:06.090
That's fine. If I get in trouble, I'll stay and fight it out. But here, I can't.

01:05:06.090 --> 01:05:07.110
Why?

01:05:07.110 --> 01:05:08.890
Because I'm supposed to represent Earth.

01:05:08.890 --> 01:05:11.220
And Earthers don't fight?

01:05:11.220 --> 01:05:15.720
Jeff, you wear that Commander's badge like you're afraid you'll break it.

01:05:15.720 --> 01:05:19.140
Okay, yes, you're supposed to speak for Earth.

01:05:19.140 --> 01:05:21.440
You're supposed to be polite and diplomatic.

01:05:21.440 --> 01:05:24.450
That doesn't mean letting them crucify you.

01:05:24.450 --> 01:05:29.380
And if you want to throw something, throw it at those bastards at Earth Central who tossed you to the wolves.

01:05:41.550 --> 01:05:55.950
You were on the line, the biggest of the Earth-Mimpari War, and you never told me.

01:06:13.280 --> 01:06:15.460
The SWAT team leader of the call came in.

01:06:18.770 --> 01:06:20.500
We all knew it was a suicide mission.

01:06:22.820 --> 01:06:25.220
The Minbari had broken through, closing in.

01:06:26.880 --> 01:06:29.440
Every ship we had left was ordered to circle Earth.

01:06:31.280 --> 01:06:32.140
We had to stop them.

01:06:32.240 --> 01:06:32.860
Hold the line.

01:06:32.960 --> 01:06:33.540
No one gets moved.

01:06:33.620 --> 01:06:34.040
No matter what.

01:06:34.290 --> 01:06:35.470
No matter what it costs.

01:06:38.190 --> 01:06:39.330
They came at us out of nowhere.

01:06:41.140 --> 01:06:42.100
We never had a chance.

01:06:42.900 --> 01:06:44.420
The sky was full of stars.

01:06:45.270 --> 01:06:47.340
And every star had been an exploding ship.

01:06:51.700 --> 01:06:54.120
My team was blown out of the sky in less than a minute.

01:07:00.440 --> 01:07:04.300
I managed to take out a fighter before they hit my stabilizers.

01:07:04.680 --> 01:07:07.180
I was losing power, lost my team.

01:07:08.780 --> 01:07:11.760
And I figured if I was going to die, I'd take some of them with me.

01:07:12.010 --> 01:07:14.130
So I targeted one of their heavy cruisers.

01:07:14.680 --> 01:07:17.260
Hit my afterburners, I was going to ram them head on.

01:07:18.040 --> 01:07:26.120
The last thing I remember is hurtling toward that cruiser, filling my screen.

01:07:30.510 --> 01:07:36.830
It's so fast in front of my eyes.

01:07:40.660 --> 01:07:42.920
I guess I blacked out from the acceleration.

01:07:45.840 --> 01:07:49.600
When I came to 24 hours later, the cruiser was gone.

01:07:52.020 --> 01:07:52.540
Checked in.

01:07:53.710 --> 01:07:55.750
Told me the war was over.

01:07:59.680 --> 01:07:59.990
Bari.

01:08:01.880 --> 01:08:03.380
Because of the line.

01:08:04.050 --> 01:08:06.660
No, that's what I'm trying to tell you.

01:08:06.980 --> 01:08:07.680
We were beaten.

01:08:08.610 --> 01:08:10.370
We didn't stop them, they stopped themselves.

01:08:12.370 --> 01:08:13.630
And I wish to hell I knew why.

01:08:15.670 --> 01:08:18.270
When we got back to Earth, everybody treated us like heroes.

01:08:19.790 --> 01:08:20.910
But we were frauds.

01:08:21.570 --> 01:08:23.490
Jeff, you are not a fraud.

01:08:24.480 --> 01:08:27.240
Anyone with enough guts to go on the line doesn't have to prove it.

01:08:31.280 --> 01:08:32.900
My whole team was wiped out.

01:08:35.110 --> 01:08:36.450
I can't let that happen again.

01:08:38.030 --> 01:08:39.450
Is that what this is about, Jeff?

01:08:40.170 --> 01:08:42.500
Are you going along with this out of guilt?

01:08:42.900 --> 01:08:45.320
Because you think history is repeating itself?

01:08:45.600 --> 01:08:47.180
Carolyn, I have a responsibility.

01:08:47.480 --> 01:08:47.980
To lead.

01:08:48.940 --> 01:08:50.660
Your team chose to go on the line.

01:08:51.380 --> 01:08:53.100
And we chose to come here.

01:08:54.110 --> 01:08:55.010
Our decision.

01:08:55.800 --> 01:08:56.860
And our risk.

01:08:57.710 --> 01:08:58.610
Not yours.

01:09:00.410 --> 01:09:07.200
if you want to stay and fight this we're with you just do what you think is right

01:09:32.110 --> 01:09:46.460
going to get some answers. Dr. Kyle. I just thought I'd stop by and see how the ambassador was doing.

01:09:48.330 --> 01:09:55.650
Definite progress. The county agent seems to be working. If we can keep his condition

01:09:55.650 --> 01:09:59.920
stable for the next few hours, he may have a chance.

01:10:09.310 --> 01:10:14.740
Lita, you saw Del Varner at the casino after the ambassador was attacked, right?

01:10:15.150 --> 01:10:16.380
Isn't that what I said?

01:10:17.860 --> 01:10:18.760
Yes, you did.

01:10:20.840 --> 01:10:22.720
And Garibaldi said the same thing.

01:10:24.340 --> 01:10:25.660
But that's what's so extraordinary.

01:10:26.950 --> 01:10:30.000
According to the autopsy of Varner's body, he's been dead.

01:10:30.000 --> 01:10:31.560
for nearly 36 hours.

01:10:32.680 --> 01:10:36.170
Meaning you and Garibaldi saw a dead man at the casino.

01:10:37.050 --> 01:10:37.710
That's it.

01:10:40.190 --> 01:10:41.330
What are you doing?

01:10:41.800 --> 01:10:43.130
Stop, you'll kill me.

01:10:44.360 --> 01:10:44.540
Oh!

01:10:44.540 --> 01:10:44.760
Oh!

01:11:19.420 --> 01:11:29.380
ambassador i think i got to him in time someone please tell me what the hell is going on around here

01:11:49.520 --> 01:11:51.700
visualize the intruder vessel, we're bringing it in.

01:12:00.700 --> 01:12:02.020
Watch your step, Commander.

01:12:02.020 --> 01:12:08.320
Repair crew found this duck to the hull at Blue 5, Level B.

01:12:08.320 --> 01:12:11.690
Destroyed a maintenance bot investigating a drop in oxygen pressure.

01:12:11.690 --> 01:12:14.530
Almost took out the repair crew before they could disable it.

01:12:14.530 --> 01:12:16.690
Looks like a transport of some kind.

01:12:16.690 --> 01:12:20.550
My guess is someone used it to fasten onto the hull and burn through into the station.

01:12:20.550 --> 01:12:22.280
How many could have come through?

01:12:22.280 --> 01:12:23.780
It's only big enough for one.

01:12:23.780 --> 01:12:27.910
I got crews checking every inch of the hull for any more, but so far, nothing.

01:12:30.000 --> 01:12:32.170
It's definitely short range.

01:12:32.170 --> 01:12:35.130
Someone had to bring this here and drop it off outside the station.

01:12:35.130 --> 01:12:39.660
Otherwise, there'd be a ship floating outside with no one in it.

01:12:39.660 --> 01:12:41.280
Exactly.

01:12:41.280 --> 01:12:43.280
Meaning someone on the station is providing support.

01:12:43.280 --> 01:12:44.140
Yeah.

01:12:44.140 --> 01:12:45.600
One other thing.

01:12:45.600 --> 01:12:48.320
