01:22:03.160 --> 01:22:07.360
Commander, this little breach of security isn't going to affect my Christmas bonus, is it?

01:22:08.130 --> 01:22:10.470
You're alright. Do you need anything?

01:22:11.420 --> 01:22:17.740
Coffee, two sugars, cream, and aspirin.

01:22:20.480 --> 01:22:23.040
Lots, lots.

01:22:34.800 --> 01:22:35.620
I wish you could stay.

01:22:36.590 --> 01:22:39.330
You just get things calmed down and you have to go.

01:22:39.850 --> 01:22:41.460
My timing always was for you.

01:22:42.290 --> 01:22:45.460
Ship's waiting.

01:22:47.040 --> 01:22:48.900
You could come with me, Jeff.

01:22:49.470 --> 01:22:51.600
We could pull our savings and buy a bigger ship.

01:22:51.680 --> 01:22:52.740
We could blow this place.

01:22:54.850 --> 01:22:56.060
I don't think about it.

01:22:58.050 --> 01:22:59.190
Well, don't take too long.

01:23:01.280 --> 01:23:04.900
- Yeah, wait, but not forever.

01:23:38.860 --> 01:23:40.570
- How's Michael?

01:23:40.570 --> 01:23:43.050
- Resting in his quarters.

01:23:43.050 --> 01:23:45.570
I checked him out pretty thoroughly.

01:23:45.570 --> 01:23:46.850
What about the station?

01:23:46.850 --> 01:23:48.280
- Holding together.

01:23:48.280 --> 01:23:51.160
I've got a repairs team working on the breach.

01:23:51.160 --> 01:23:54.720
It'll take a few days, but it's nothing we can't fix.

01:23:54.720 --> 01:23:57.530
- Good.

01:23:57.530 --> 01:24:00.000
You can tell the Volons that Ambassador Clark

01:24:00.000 --> 01:24:05.600
is out of critical the cadre agent worked even better than I had hoped

01:24:05.600 --> 01:24:23.200
commander may I speak with you I studied a record of your confrontation I

01:24:23.200 --> 01:24:28.700
regret that Aminbari was responsible for all this sadness you can't be

01:24:28.700 --> 01:24:30.000
responsible for the action

01:24:30.000 --> 01:24:31.460
of every one of your race, Dylan.

01:24:31.960 --> 01:24:35.500
No, but there is something I can do.

01:24:37.120 --> 01:24:39.440
I recognized the markings on his face

01:24:39.440 --> 01:24:41.900
and I was able to determine who

01:24:41.900 --> 01:24:43.440
and what he was.

01:24:44.690 --> 01:24:47.420
I just received this file

01:24:47.420 --> 01:24:48.590
from my government.

01:24:49.850 --> 01:24:52.440
A full record of his travels.

01:24:54.020 --> 01:24:55.240
I think you will find it

01:24:55.240 --> 01:24:57.700
most interesting.

01:24:59.380 --> 01:25:00.000
So, Doctor,

01:25:01.210 --> 01:25:03.610
Just what did you see when you looked inside that suit?

01:25:03.610 --> 01:25:23.580
There are moments in your life when everything crystallizes and the whole world reshapes itself right down to its component molecules and everything changes.

01:25:26.040 --> 01:25:29.540
I have looked upon the face of a fallen creature.

01:25:33.450 --> 01:25:51.180
nothing is the same anymore. You wanted to see me, Commander? I thought you might like

01:25:51.180 --> 01:26:00.000
to join me in a toast before the reception. Ambassador Jakar? To fully operation

01:26:00.000 --> 01:26:03.180
Babylon 5. To the future.

01:26:07.690 --> 01:26:09.310
I'm pleased that the Vorlongs have

01:26:09.310 --> 01:26:11.050
dropped all charges against you

01:26:11.050 --> 01:26:13.110
now that the real culprit has been

01:26:13.110 --> 01:26:14.830
found. Have you

01:26:14.830 --> 01:26:17.620
learned anything more about him? Yes.

01:26:18.740 --> 01:26:20.220
Our would-be assassin had an interesting

01:26:20.220 --> 01:26:22.520
background. Seems he belonged to

01:26:22.520 --> 01:26:24.440
a branch of the Minbari warrior caste

01:26:24.440 --> 01:26:26.340
who split from their government after the war.

01:26:26.620 --> 01:26:27.760
A warrior caste?

01:26:28.160 --> 01:26:30.000
That explains why he would want to destroy

01:26:30.000 --> 01:26:34.460
disrupt Babylon 5 and our mutual goal of peace.

01:26:34.460 --> 01:26:38.080
I'm surprised you didn't ask about Delvarner.

01:26:38.080 --> 01:26:40.850
I assumed he was simply another innocent victim.

01:26:40.850 --> 01:26:42.780
Not quite.

01:26:42.780 --> 01:26:47.560
We checked his ship's logs and apparently he spent a lot of time working for your government.

01:26:47.560 --> 01:26:51.670
A lucrative business running forbidden technology into Narn space.

01:26:51.670 --> 01:26:56.550
His last entry spoke of a big payoff for bringing a changeling net across the border.

01:26:56.550 --> 01:27:00.000
He was supposed to meet with his buyer in the tiger sector but was running behind.

01:27:00.030 --> 01:27:04.150
Didn't your supply ship also pass through the Tigris sector on its way here?

01:27:04.150 --> 01:27:08.400
If you have a point to make, Commander, please make it.

01:27:08.400 --> 01:27:15.060
I believe the Assassin was brought here on your supply ship. That's why they needed the

01:27:15.060 --> 01:27:21.230
Changeling net before they arrived. A Manbari warrior walking off a Narn ship would draw

01:27:21.230 --> 01:27:26.420
a lot of attention. With the net, he could appear to be one of your crew and infiltrate

01:27:26.420 --> 01:27:30.000
the station. When Varner missed connecting with your

01:27:30.030 --> 01:27:35.490
ship he came here so you had to find another way to get the assassin on board they used the

01:27:35.490 --> 01:27:41.120
transport we found on the station's hull to get him inside he then killed delvarner and grabbed

01:27:41.120 --> 01:27:47.700
the changeling net sheer speculation commander with the death of delvarner and of the assassin

01:27:47.700 --> 01:28:00.000
you have no proof that's right well i should be on my way one more thing as i mentioned

01:28:00.060 --> 01:28:02.960
The assassin belonged to the Minbari warrior class.

01:28:02.960 --> 01:28:06.380
During the war, I was in my world's warrior class.

01:28:06.380 --> 01:28:11.000
We saved each other's lives a dozen times over, made the sort of friendships that last

01:28:11.000 --> 01:28:12.430
a lifetime.

01:28:12.430 --> 01:28:13.430
Commendable!

01:28:13.430 --> 01:28:15.730
But what does that have to do with...

01:28:15.730 --> 01:28:16.730
With nanotechnology?

01:28:16.730 --> 01:28:17.810
Glad you asked.

01:28:17.810 --> 01:28:19.670
You've heard of it, haven't you?

01:28:19.670 --> 01:28:22.030
Machines too small for the human eye to see.

01:28:22.030 --> 01:28:26.810
You can even shield them, make them invisible to electronic detection.

01:28:26.810 --> 01:28:28.800
Like the one you just swallowed in that drink.

01:28:31.120 --> 01:28:34.520
I imagine it's firmly latched onto your intestinal tract by now.

01:28:34.520 --> 01:28:38.980
Well, it's nothing harmful, Ambassador.

01:28:38.980 --> 01:28:45.080
It's a location transmitter, see?

01:28:45.080 --> 01:28:48.610
It should dissolve in about five years.

01:28:48.610 --> 01:28:51.340
But until then, Ambassador,

01:28:51.340 --> 01:28:55.780
my friends in my warrior cast have this frequency.

01:28:55.780 --> 01:28:58.330
And if anything should happen to Babylon 5,

01:28:58.330 --> 01:29:00.000
they have instructions to track down

01:29:00.030 --> 01:29:08.800
that transmitter and well why spoil the surprise this is an outrage this is insurance what you do

01:29:08.800 --> 01:29:13.580
here is your own business you can scheme and plan and play all the games you want but get this

01:29:13.580 --> 01:29:18.660
